    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG are delighted to present 17 Osprey Drive, a superbly extended and beautifully finished four bed (plus excellent converted attic room) semi-detached family home, ideally positioned within a highly sought-after residential cul-de-sac. Thoughtfully upgraded and meticulously maintained, this exceptional property offers a perfect blend of contemporary style and practical family living. Presented in immaculate, turnkey condition, no expense has been spared by its current owners in creating a home of outstanding quality and comfort. From the moment you step inside, the high-quality finish, tasteful décor and attention to detail are immediately evident. The property offers both functionality and visual appeal, creating a warm and inviting atmosphere suited to modern family life as well as entertaining. This is a home of true distinction, set in one of South Dublin's most desirable and established family locations. Further enhancing its appeal, the property boasts an impressive C2 BER rating, ensuring excellent energy efficiency and year-round comfort.\n\nHeavily extended and modernised in recent years, this home offers bright, spacious and well-balanced accommodation. The ground floor comprises a large welcoming entrance hallway, an elegant front sitting room, second lounge/playroom, a stunning beautifully appointed kitchen/dining/family room extension that forms the heart of the home and an enviable utility room and shower room off. Upstairs, there are four generously proportioned bedrooms and a family bathroom, while the converted attic level (completed c. 2017) provides a versatile additional space, ideal for a home office/study, music room, playroom or guest accommodation. Outside, the property continues to impress with a private, low-maintenance rear garden—perfect for outdoor dining and entertaining—while the front features a recently paved driveway with convenient off-street parking for two vehicles.\n \nLocated in one of South Dublin's most desirable residential areas, Osprey is a most popular and well-established estate offering a superb range of highly regarded schools within walking distance including Bishop Galvin and Bishop Shanahan NS, St Mac Dara's, Templeogue College, Terenure College, Presentation Terenure, St. Pius X and Our Lady's Secondary School. There are numerous local green spaces and the facilities at the wonderful Tymon Park are on its doorstep (with access from the rear of the estate). This area is extremely family friendly with numerous local sport establishments — Faughs GAA Club, St. Judes GAA Club, Templeogue United Football Club, St. Mary's College RFC, Templeogue Swimming Club and Templeogue Tennis Club. There is convenient shopping nearby with Orwell Shopping centre just around the corner and the area is also well serviced by public transport. The Osprey estate also offers quick and easy access to both the M50 road network and the city centre. Viewing is a must to see what this fantastic property has to offer."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nGround Floor - \n\n\nEntrance Hall - 5.46m × 1.81m\n\n\nLiving Room - 5.46m × 3.55m\n\n\nStudy Room - 5.11m × 1.99m\n\n\nKitchen/Dining/Family Room - 8.79m × 5.45m\n\n\nUitility Room - 2.63m × 1.99m\n\n\nShower Room/WC - 1.38m × 1.99m\n\n\nFirst Floor - \n\n\nBedroom 1 - 4.21m × 3.27m\n\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.26m × 3.27m\n\n\nBedroom 3 - 4.30m × 1.99m\n\n\nBedroom 4 - 3.17m × 4.39m\n\n\nBathroom - 1.88m × 2.09m\n\n\nAttic Level - \n\n\nAttic Room 1 - 3.70m × 3.13m\n\n\nAttic Room 2 - 3.70m × 4.31m\n\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Beautifully finished, most-substantial 4 bed/2 bath (plus attic) semi-detached family home</li><li> 181 sqm. / 1,948 sq.ft. approx. (including excellent converted walk-in attic space)</li><li> Recently re-configured to the highest of standards; including front and rear/side extensions (2007) and converted walk-in attic space (2017)</li><li> GFCH</li><li> Modern double glazing throughout, plus composite front door</li><li> Off-street parking</li><li> Security alarm</li><li> Rear block-built shed</li><li> Most sought-after family orientated estate</li><li> Close to an array of excellent schools, sports and recreation clubs, shops, villages and transport links.</li><li> Tymon Park and all its wonderful facilities are on its doorstep, with access from the rear of the estate</li><li> Excellent buses servicing the area</li><li> Just minutes from the M50 road network, connecting all major national routes</li><li> C2 BER rating.</ul>"
      },
